{"kind":"request","text":"The fold refuses a genesis whose seed names another definition, so a replica cannot fold one scope's journal under another scope's rules.\n\nFiled 2026-11-13 07:43 EST at Hugh's request, from the dap-foldkit M2 reviews. Every dap fact below is read at main `64112e45`.\n\n## Ask\n\nIn `applyEntry` (`packages/derive/src/fold.ts:58`), for a genesis entry whose `input.seed.definition` is a digest, throw `FoldError` when that digest differs from `definition.digest`.\n\n## Why\n\n`judgeGenesis` makes this check before it writes a genesis (`packages/derive/src/genesis.ts:127`, \"the seed names another definition\"). `applyEntry` does not make it. A caller that folds a journal with the wrong `ValidDefinition` gets no error from the genesis. The fold then fails at some later entry, or it does not fail and holds a wrong state.\n\nInside dap, each caller of `applyEntry` holds the definition that the scope's own genesis pinned. A replica in a browser takes its definition from the page's build and its entries from the network. The dap-foldkit replica (`~/play/dap-foldkit/lib/replica/replica.ts`, `fold`) makes no check of its own. A page built for one definition and pointed at a scope of another predicts with the wrong rules and reports no fault.\n\n`declaredHandle` (`packages/client/src/declared.ts`) refuses `definition-mismatch` from the summary, and `ScopeHandle.log` checks each page against the summary. Both checks depend on the path that the entries came by. The check in the fold holds for every path.\n\n## Size and priority\n\nSmall: one comparison, one test for a declared definition, one test that a platform definition name still folds. Low priority. It belongs before the replica moves into `packages/client`.\n\n## Filing rule\n\nThe request adds no scope kind, no platform definition name, no capability, no tool family and no record model. The fold refuses an entry that no judge writes, as it does for an entry that does not follow the head.\n\nSource: `~/play/dap-foldkit/PLAN.md`, draft 3, revision 6, section 8.3, row D10.","body":{"conditions":"applyEntry throws FoldError for a genesis whose seed names a definition digest other than definition.digest. One test folds a genesis under another declared definition and expects the error. A genesis that names a platform definition folds as before. npm run gate passes.","target":"inherit","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}